findings.body:
**Same factual error, duplicated in code.** The comment says:

```ts
// The store is not always the caller's own since the fleet views
// (decisions 60, 61), and `pup ui` draws the backlog, the ledger and
// the radar, which the fleet `pup status` does not: every id is
// scrubbed like the session row's.
id: sanitizeReason(task.id),
```

"the ledger … which the fleet `pup status` does not [draw]" is false: `printFleet` (the fleet `pup status`) loops over `snapshot.overdueDebt` and prints `entry.id` directly, a few lines below this same function (`overdueDebt: listOverdueLedgerEntries(...).map((entry) => ({ id: sanitizeReason(String(entry.id)), ... }))`). This sits right next to the code it describes, making the inaccuracy easy to trip over when reasoning about which sanitization protects which command.

Permalink: https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/f901f16ff87fefe4fe2b20077b69f4e1280330b2/src/core/dashboard.service.ts#L79-L82

